      "refersTo": "adult-dialog",
      "description": "The visible adult surface with fixed-style heading and footer framing a settings section; this specimen is not a functional modal.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-dialog\" aria-labelledby=\"ds-dialog-title\"><header class=\"ds-dialog-heading\"><div><h2 id=\"ds-dialog-title\">Eure ruhige Nacht</h2><p>So, wie es zu euch passt.</p></div><button class=\"ds-close\" aria-label=\"Zur Geschichte zurück\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 6 12 12M6 18 18 6\"/></svg></button></header><div class=\"ds-dialog-scroll\"><section class=\"ds-dialog-section\"><h3>Hören</h3><label class=\"ds-dialog-toggle\"><span>Erzählertext anzeigen</span><input type=\"checkbox\" checked></label></section></div><footer class=\"ds-dialog-footer\"><button class=\"ds-dialog-done\">Zurück in den Wald <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6\"/></svg></button></footer></section>",
      "css": ".ds-dialog{font-family:Schlafwald,'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;background:var(--panel,#f4efdf);color:var(--ink,#28433f);border-radius:20px;box-shadow:0 24px 90px rgba(8,25,23,.3);width:min(780px,calc(100vw - 40px));max-width:100%;overflow:hidden;text-align:left}.ds-dialog-heading{padding:26px 32px 18px;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px solid #d6dcca}.ds-dialog-heading h2{font-family:Lora,Georgia,serif;font-size:30px;line-height:1.18;letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:400;margin:0 0 10px}.ds-dialog-heading p{margin:0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#51665a}.ds-close{color:#567061;background:transparent;border:0;min-width:48px;min-height:48px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border-radius:50%;cursor:pointer;margin:-6px -12px 0 0}.ds-close svg{width:21px;height:21px}.ds-dialog-scroll{padding:0 32px;max-height:calc(100dvh - 230px);overflow-y:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;scrollbar-width:thin;scrollbar-color:#91a187 #eeeada}.ds-dialog-section{padding:24px 0}.ds-dialog-section h3{font-size:17px;margin:0 0 20px;color:#304d3c}.ds-dialog-toggle{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;min-height:56px;font-size:14px;cursor:pointer}.ds-dialog-toggle input{accent-color:#516e54;min-width:24px;min-height:24px;margin:0;cursor:pointer}.ds-dialog-toggle input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a97947;outline-offset:4px}.ds-dialog-footer{padding:16px 32px 22px;border-top:1px solid #d6dcca;display:flex;justify-content:flex-end}.ds-dialog-done{font-family:Schlafwald,'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;background:#49654e;color:#fbf2de;min-height:52px;padding:14px 23px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:20px;border:0;border-radius:27px;font-weight:800;font-size:14px;box-shadow:0 8px 22px rgba(16,35,32,.16);cursor:pointer}.ds-dialog-done svg{width:21px;height:21px}.ds-close:hover{filter:brightness(1.05)}.ds-close:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-close:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a97947;outline-offset:4px}.ds-close:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:default}.ds-dialog-done:hover{filter:brightness(1.05)}.ds-dialog-done:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-dialog-done:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a97947;outline-offset:4px}.ds-dialog-done:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:default}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Animal journey strip",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "journey",
      "description": "Passive status strip showing sleeping, current and waiting animals; it contains no navigation actions.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-journey\" aria-label=\"Die Tiere dieser Nacht\"><span class=\"ds-asleep\"><i></i><span>Fino</span></span><span class=\"ds-current\"><i></i><span>Mila</span></span><span><i></i><span>Piko</span></span><span><i></i><span>Luna</span></span><span><i></i><span>Nuri</span></span><span><i></i><span>Leni</span></span><span><i></i><span>Suri</span></span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-journey{font-family:Schlafwald,'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;display:flex;gap:24px;pointer-events:none}.ds-journey>span{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:11px;color:#bcc9b9}.ds-journey i{display:block;width:6px;height:6px;background:#b5bdad;border-radius:50%;opacity:.45}.ds-journey .ds-current i{background:#f4d6a3;opacity:1;box-shadow:0 0 14px rgba(241,214,159,.5)}.ds-journey .ds-asleep i{opacity:.7;background:#aac3aa}.ds-journey .ds-current{color:#f3dfbc}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Gesture instruction",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "gesture",
      "description": "Non-interactive leaf capsule that gives one gentle instruction above narration.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-gesture\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M19 4C10 2 3 6 5 14c2 8 13 5 14-10Z\"/><path d=\"M5 20 15 9\"/></svg><span>Bring es ganz sanft zum leuchtenden Platz.</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-gesture{font-family:Schlafwald,'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:rgba(32,55,47,.88);color:#e8e8cf;padding:10px 16px;border-radius:24px;font-size:13px;max-width:75vw;pointer-events:none}.ds-gesture svg{width:20px;height:20px;color:#f1d3a1;flex:none}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Animal checkbox row",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "checkbox-row",
      "description": "Native checkbox inside a generous animal label; the smaller species text uses the reviewed contrast color.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-animal-option\"><input type=\"checkbox\" checked><span>Fino<small>der Fuchs</small></span></label>",
      "css": ".ds-animal-option{font-family:Schlafwald,'Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;min-height:66px;color:var(--ink,#28433f);cursor:pointer}.ds-animal-option input{accent-color:#516e54;min-width:24px;min-height:24px;margin:0;cursor:pointer}.ds-animal-option input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a97947;outline-offset:4px}.ds-animal-option span{font-size:15px}.ds-animal-option small{display:block;font-size:11px;color:#586b52;margin-top:3px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The quiet storybook clearing",
    "overview": "The world is a soft, genuine three-dimensional forest at dusk. Rounded animal bodies, cream faces, rose and peach details, moss islands, overlapping trees and small points of warm light create the children's storybook character. The forest carries the experience; the interface stays sparse and leaves the animals visible at a child's eye level.\n\nWarm display lettering and rounded body text keep the small amount of language gentle. Adult controls occupy a separate cream dialog with dark green text, native form fields and clear keyboard focus. This records the implemented browser world in `WebApp/src/style.css`, `world.js` and `main.js`, checked against the final welcome and parent captures; it is not a replacement direction for the retained Unity project.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A continuous forest image with restrained text overlays.",
      "Soft mesh silhouettes with distinct animal anatomy and sleep gestures.",
      "Cream, moss, peach and rose held against a cool evening atmosphere.",
      "Large, rounded actions and a protected, readable adult dialog."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Forest First Rule",
        "body": "Use scene materials to establish the world; reserve interface color for readable text, gentle actions and adult controls.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Story Voice Rule",
        "body": "Use Lora for story and dialog headings and Nunito for controls, body copy and labels; keep the welcome hierarchy beginning with its heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Soft Depth Rule",
        "body": "Use overlapping geometry, tonal separation and diffuse shadows; retain the rounded, calm material character of the forest.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the animal and its sleep-place visible beneath sparse overlays.",
      "Do use self-hosted Lora headings and Nunito body text with the recorded roles.",
      "Do preserve the current readable species-label color on the cream adult panel.",
      "Do keep large action targets, visible keyboard focus and the adult dialog's native form controls.",
      "Do use softly curved meshes and distinct anatomy when extending the animal world."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add an eyebrow above the welcome heading or copy the letter-spaced wordmark into section labels.",
      "Don't replace the live three-dimensional forest with a flat concept image or billboard animals.",
      "Don't introduce bloom, hard real-time shadows or sharp bedding into this soft scene language.",
      "Don't turn the passive journey strip into a score, reward meter or competitive progress treatment.",
      "Don't treat the CSS reduced-motion rule as proof that scene motion or physical-device behavior has been validated."
    ]
  }
}
